#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is &kappname;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&kappname; is an image viewer for &kde;."
msgid "&kappname; is a fast and easy to use image viewer for KDE."
msgstr "O &kappname; é un visor de imaxes para o &kde;."

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Gwenview features three main modes: Browse, View, and Full Screen. Browse "
"Mode lets you navigate through your computer showing thumbnails of your "
"images, View Mode lets you view images one at a time, and Full Screen lets "
"you make quick slideshows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Image loading is handled by the Qt library, so &kappname; supports all image "
"formats your Qt installation supports. &kappname; correctly displays images "
"with an alpha channel (transparency) as well as animations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; supports the displaying and editing of EXIF comments in JPEG "
"images. Lossless JPEG transforms such as rotations and mirroring are also "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "The interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "Image Operations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Gwenview has a few features which are available in both Browse, View, and "
"Full Screen view. Gwenview has the capability to do basic alteration of your "
"images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Rotate: A rotate operation will rotate the image either to the left or to "
"the right, depending on whether you do <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Rotate Right</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> or <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;"
"<keycap>L</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Rotate Left</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Mirror</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>: This operation will reflect the image along the vertical axis, "
"as if you were seeing it in a mirror."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Flip</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>: This operation will reflect the image upside-down (a reflection "
"along the horizontal axis)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Resize</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>: This operation will allow you to shrink or expand the image. "
"Note that if you increase the size of an image, it may appear blurry and/or "
"pixelated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Crop</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>: This operation lets you discard parts of the image you don't "
"want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browse Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When in Browse Mode, you can easily navigate through your files and folders. "
"The preview window shows thumbnails of the images in the current folder, as "
"well as subfolders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browse Mode Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Moving the mouse over an image shows buttons to rotate the image as well as "
"a button to enter Fullscreen Mode. Clicking on an image takes you into View "
"Mode. The sidebar on the right does not appear by default, but its "
"appearance can be toggled using <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycap>F11</keycap> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show/Hide Sidebar</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> or using the <guiicon>Show/Hide Sidebar</guiicon> "
"button. Note that the option will appear as either <guiicon>Show Sidebar</"
"guiicon> or <guiicon>Hide Sidebar</guiicon>, depending on whether the "
"sidebar is currently shown. The slider at the bottom right allows you to "
"change the size of the image thumbnails. You can also filter the images by "
"filename using the box on the lower left. The toolbar (left) appears in both "
"Browse mode as well as View mode and contains the most commonly used actions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browse: Switches to Browse Mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "View: Switches to View Mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Screen: Switches to Full Screen Mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Go to Previous Image: Clicking this icon will go to the previous image in "
"the folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Go to Next Image: Clicking this button will go to the next image in the "
"folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rotate Left/Right: Same as discussed in Image Operations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show Sidebar: Shows the sidebar (right) which displays information about the "
"current image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"View Mode displays one image at a time. At the bottom, there is the "
"Thumbnail Bar, which allows you to scroll through the images in the current "
"folder. The Thumbnail Bar can be minimized by clicking on the Thumbnail Bar "
"button. Clicking again will restore it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "View Mode Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The slider at the bottom right controls the zoom of the image. The "
"<guiicon>Zoom to Fit</guiicon> button and the <guiicon>Actual Size</guiicon> "
"button are next to the zoom slider and are two preset zoom levels. The "
"<guiicon>Zoom to Fit</guiicon> button zooms the current image to fit the "
"size of the window, and the <guiicon>Actual Size</guiicon> button zooms the "
"image to the actual pixel size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can start directly in View mode by starting &kappname; from a context "
"menu like Open With in another program or by launching it from the command "
"line with an image as an argument."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Screen Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Full Screen Mode shows a slideshow of your images. Access Full Screen "
"Mode by clicking on the button that appears when you move the mouse over the "
"thumbnails in Browse Mode, by pressing the <guiicon>Full Screen</guiicon> "
"button on the taskbar, or by <menuchoice> <shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>View</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Full Screen Mode</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Screen Mode Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top bar will hide itself automatically; to show it simply move the mouse "
"to the top of the screen. If the mouse cursor is over the top bar, it will "
"not autohide. Most of the buttons on the bar are the same as the ones on the "
"toolbar in Browse or View Modes, except for the <guiicon>Exit Full Screen "
"Mode</guiicon> button which returns you to the &kappname; window, the "
"<guiicon>Start/Stop Slideshow</guiicon> button, and the <guiicon>Configure "
"Full Screen Mode</guiicon> button which shows a small settings dialog that "
"allows you to easily and quickly configure the slideshow. The slideshow "
"controls there are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Interval slider controls how long &kappname; will show an image before "
"it move to the next one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the Loop checkbox is checked, when the end of the slideshow is reached, "
"it will continue from the beginning instead of stopping."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the Random checkbox is checked, instead of progressing through the folder "
"alphabetically, images will be shown in random order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Also in the top bar is an area that shows you the other images in the "
"current folder. Clicking on one will display it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tips"
msgstr "Suxestións"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid "Panning with the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Holding down the left mouse button on an image allows you to scroll the "
"image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "The mouse wheel will scroll the image up and down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Zooming with the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clicking the middle mouse button will toggle the auto zoom on/off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hold down the Control key, then either use the mouse wheel to zoom in and "
"out or left click to zoom in and right click to zoom out."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mouse wheel, used while holding down the Alt key, will scroll the image "
"horizontally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "Browsing with the mouse"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When in Browse mode, clicking an image switches into View mode and shows "
"that image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When in Browse mode, scrolling the mouse wheel will scroll up or down the "
"thumbail view area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the Mouse Behaviour option in <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kappname;</guimenuitem></menuchoice> is set "
"to Browse, scrolling the mouse wheel while in View Mode will move you "
"through the images in the folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:326
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&mouse; &keybindings;"
msgid "Key bindings"
msgstr "&mouse; &keybindings;"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; comes with a range of keyboard shortcuts, all of which can be "
"viewed and remapped by selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Note "
"that in the Files and Folders windows, all the normal KDE shortcuts are "
"functional, unless otherwise remapped."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "A few of the most useful default bindings are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Space</keycap>: Displays the next image in the directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Backspace;: Displays the previous image in the directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>Up</keycap></keycombo>: Moves to the "
"parent folder of the current folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>: "
"Switches into Full Screen Mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Esc;: Exits from Full Screen mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap></keycombo>: Show or hide "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>B</keycap></keycombo>: Show or hide "
"the Thumbnail bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>F11</keycap> Show or hide the Sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycap>F6</keycap> Make the Location bar editable so that you can directly "
"type in a file path. You can return to the standard Location Bar by pressing "
"the arrow at the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo>: Rotate the "
"current image to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>L</keycap></keycombo>: Rotate the "
"current image to the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo>: Save any "
"changes made to the image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Del</keycap> Move the current image to the trash."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>Del</keycap></keycombo>: "
"Permenantly delete the image from the disk. Note that this operation is "
"irreversible and cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>: Print the "
"current image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo>: Open an "
"image using the standard file selection dialog."
msgstr ""
